      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "προσκυνῶν ὑμᾶς καὶ θύων καὶ σπένδων καὶ τῆς ὑμετέρας μεταλαμβάνων τραπέζης ἢ ἕτερόν τι ὧν οὐ χρὴ ἐκτελῶν ἢ αἷμα χέων ἢ σαρκῶν νεκρῶν γευόμενος",
          "english_quote": "by worshiping you, sacrificing, pouring libations, sharing in your table, doing anything else that ought not to be done, shedding blood, tasting dead flesh",
          "issue": "The draft flattens the initial καί-linked sequence and the subsequent ἤ-linked alternatives into one comma-separated list governed by the later 'or.' This obscures the source's coordination pattern within the description of self-enslavement. Preserving that pattern need not settle whether every initial ritual act is required together.",
          "suggested_revision": "Render the sequence as 'by worshiping you and sacrificing and pouring libations and sharing in your table, or doing anything else that ought not to be done, or shedding blood, or tasting dead flesh,' continuing with the remaining alternatives. Do not add an explanation asserting that all the initial acts are jointly necessary.",
